  "digest": "# Industrials digest \u2014 week 2026-W46\n\n## Coverage changes\n\nSeven industrials names published this week, all updates of existing coverage. Astra International (ASII) stays HOLD at Rp4,692, with its automotive business supported by Gaikindo\u2019s reported 760,476 unit January\u2013October wholesales (up 35.5% year\u2011on\u2011year) [2026-11-07 news bafbe92a, 226d14c2]. Astra\u2019s financial\u2011services arm FIFGROUP noted improved motorcycle\u2011finance NPLs versus last year [2026-11-12 news 2322520f]. United Tractors (UNTR) issued a BUY at Rp47,305 citing heavy\u2011equipment demand from coal mining. The other conglomerates \u2013 Alam Tri Resources (ADRO, HOLD Rp2,118, aluminium\u2011smelter contribution cited in Q3\u20112026 results [2026-11-10 news d189ed7f]), Nusantara Infrastructure (ITMA, REDUCE Rp905), DSSA (SELL Rp416), IMAS (SELL Rp458) and Benakat Petroleum (BNBR, HOLD Rp38.44) \u2013 retain their ratings; DSSA appears on OJK\u2019s published list of trading\u2011case violators [2026-11-07 news 2c8818cf]. ADRO and parent Adaro Energy (AADI) recorded a jumbo crossing transaction valued at about Rp66\u202ftrillion [2026-11-10 news b555e015, 2026-11-11 news 71e9a110].\n\n## Deck moves\n\nThe macro, metals and agri decks\u2019 timestamps advanced to 13\u202fNovember, reflecting routine daily refresh of forward prices and inflation series; no substantive changes this week.\n\n## Material news\n\n\u2013 OJK published its list of violators in the DSSA, BREN and CUAN trading cases [2026-11-07 news 2c8818cf].\n\u2013 Gaikindo industry data shows January\u2011October 2026 car wholesales reached 760,476 units (up 35.5% y/y) and motorcycle sales 5.65\u202fmillion units (up 4.17% y/y), on track for the 850,000\u2011unit annual target [2026-11-09 news dc226ac48e629799, 2026-11-10 news 4e693b3b1fd15e25].\n\u2013 ADRO recorded a jumbo negotiated\u2011market crossing valued at ~Rp66\u202ftrillion; control stakes were transferred to four linked companies [2026-11-10 news b555e015, 2026-11-11 news 71e9a110].\n\u2013 Gaikindo Auto Week 2026 runs 20\u201329\u202fNovember in ten cities, aiming to sustain sales momentum [2026-11-09 news 9d3910cee20eda56].\n\u2013 October 2026 unit sales: Toyota led brands, BYD moved into third place overtaking Suzuki and Honda [2026-11-10 news fe6e48a6c1f6f5b1].\n\n## Watch next week\n\nMonitor Gaikindo Auto Week 2026 (20\u201329\u202fNov) for year\u2011end sales\u2011event impact and any update to the 2027 industry target. ADRO\u2019s aluminium\u2011smelter ramp\u2011up post\u2011Q3 growth [2026-11-10 news d189ed7f] and trading\u2011volume pattern after the Rp66\u202ftrillion crossing. Year\u2011end industry data releases and early\u20112027 outlook statements.\n\n*Research only; not a recommendation to act.*",
